faq:
  - q: "Is this website audit free?"
    a: "Yes. Enter any public website address and the examination runs on the engine at no cost, with no account. Public use is rate-limited per visitor to keep it available."
  - q: "What does the audit check?"
    a: "Eight areas: technical structure, SEO tags and files, performance including Core Web Vitals, accessibility markup, security headers, a sample of links, content, and AI visibility. Each finding shows its evidence and a fix."
  - q: "Is the score the same as Google PageSpeed or Lighthouse?"
    a: "No. Vector's health score covers eight areas, of which page speed is one. Its Core Web Vitals figures come from Google PageSpeed Insights, using real-user data when the site has enough traffic and a lab run otherwise, so those numbers match what Google reports."
  - q: "What does the AI visibility score measure?"
    a: "Whether AI answer crawlers such as ChatGPT search, Perplexity, and Claude are allowed to read the site, whether it publishes structured data and an llms.txt file, and whether its text is readable without JavaScript. It does not query any AI product, so it cannot tell you whether an answer currently mentions the site."
  - q: "Can I download the report?"
    a: "Yes. Every report has a permanent link, a Save as PDF button, and a Download CSV button with the scores and every issue, ready for a spreadsheet."
  - q: "Can I share the report?"
    a: "Every examination gets a permanent link. Send it to a colleague or a client, or save it as a PDF from the report."
  - q: "Will my website appear on the recently examined list?"
    a: "Only if you leave the listing option on when you run it. Untick it and the domain and score are kept private to the report link."
